63
00:04:03,980 --> 00:04:05,980
I would think it obvious.

64
00:04:07,980 --> 00:04:10,980
It's obvious you're a sadistic man, Stein.

65
00:04:13,980 --> 00:04:14,980
I want to dissect.

66
00:04:14,980 --> 00:04:22,980
Dead or alive in the rift between Revival and Dazzlement?

67
00:04:25,980 --> 00:04:29,980
Oh Stein, you're so adorable.

68
00:04:31,980 --> 00:04:32,980
Yeah.

69
00:04:32,980 --> 00:04:36,980
I almost forgot it's my job to control this head case.

70
00:04:37,980 --> 00:04:38,980
What's this fool up to now?

71
00:04:41,980 --> 00:04:43,980
Please, no more. I'm begging you.

72
00:04:44,980 --> 00:04:46,980
I'm gonna tear you into little pieces.

73
00:04:47,980 --> 00:04:48,980
I wonder how I should do it though.

74
00:04:49,980 --> 00:04:52,980
Cut up or gouge out or simply rip apart.

75
00:04:53,980 --> 00:04:54,980
That's for later though.

76
00:04:55,980 --> 00:04:57,980
Right now I'll give you a painless death.

77
00:05:00,980 --> 00:05:01,980
Step away.

78
00:05:02,980 --> 00:05:04,980
I think that's enough, don't you?

79
00:05:05,980 --> 00:05:06,980
Stay out of this spirit.

80
00:05:07,980 --> 00:05:09,980
I'm going to do things my way.

81
00:05:10,980 --> 00:05:11,980
So then what?

82
00:05:12,980 --> 00:05:14,980
You're just going to ignore all the Academy's rules?

83
00:05:18,980 --> 00:05:19,980
Well, what is it you want to do?

84
00:05:20,980 --> 00:05:24,980
Did you think you could simply do anything you please once you were in the DWMA?

85
00:05:25,980 --> 00:05:28,980
I wish I lived in a world that knew nothing of the gods.

86
00:05:28,980 --> 00:05:29,980
Whoa, whoa.

87
00:05:29,980 --> 00:05:31,980
Do you seriously mean that?

88
00:05:32,980 --> 00:05:33,980
Of course not.

89
00:05:34,980 --> 00:05:35,980
A world like that would be...

90
00:05:36,980 --> 00:05:37,980
diseased.

91
00:05:38,980 --> 00:05:41,980
I'll say it again, Professor Stein.

92
00:05:42,980 --> 00:05:43,980
Join my experiment.

93
00:05:44,980 --> 00:05:47,980
This static, unchanging world doesn't suit you.

94
00:05:48,980 --> 00:05:49,980
You were made for better than this.

95
00:05:50,980 --> 00:05:51,980
You're a scientist after all.

96
00:05:52,980 --> 00:05:54,980
We can harness the power of the Kishin together.

97
00:05:55,980 --> 00:05:57,980
We'll change the world back to what it should be.

98
00:05:58,980 --> 00:06:01,980
A place where evolution and progress always reign.

99
00:06:02,980 --> 00:06:03,980
A long time ago.

100
00:06:04,980 --> 00:06:11,980
I was analyzed by a group of foolish doctors who feared my violent tendencies and what they considered my selfish attitude.

101
00:06:12,980 --> 00:06:14,980
They seemed elated while they were studying me.

102
00:06:15,980 --> 00:06:19,980
As if they were solving the crime in a mystery novel they theorized for hours.

103
00:06:20,980 --> 00:06:22,980
Wondering if something had traumatized me in my past.

104
00:06:23,980 --> 00:06:26,980
Or if some terrible influence had come into my life.

105
00:06:26,980 --> 00:06:31,980
That was all nonsense though.

106
00:06:32,980 --> 00:06:34,980
I've loved tearing things apart from the very beginning.

107
00:06:35,980 --> 00:06:36,980
What's your point, Stein?

108
00:06:36,980 --> 00:06:38,980
Are you trying to compare me to these doctors?

109
00:06:40,980 --> 00:06:46,980
When I was in kindergarten it made me nauseous watching the other kids as they listened dutifully to the teacher and played games.

110
00:06:46,980 --> 00:06:53,980
I would almost puke just from the sight of everyone focusing unquestioningly on the chalkboard while they took their notes.

111
00:06:54,980 --> 00:06:55,980
Not an original thought in their heads.

112
00:06:56,980 --> 00:06:57,980
What kind of story is this anyway?

113
00:06:58,980 --> 00:07:00,980
It's entirely pointless not to mention boring.

114
00:07:01,980 --> 00:07:02,980
Makes me want to puke.

115
00:07:02,980 --> 00:07:15,980
Are you mocking me?

116
00:07:16,980 --> 00:07:19,980
If you hate unoriginality so much why are your attacks so tiresome?

117
00:07:20,980 --> 00:07:22,980
Really, I'm sleeping here.

118
00:07:23,980 --> 00:07:24,980
Now, now, be more patient.

119
00:07:25,980 --> 00:07:28,980
This is my answer to your invitation so you should listen.

120
00:07:28,980 --> 00:07:33,980
My feelings didn't change as I matured and grew stronger.

121
00:07:33,980 --> 00:07:36,980
The madness inside of me, the desire to dissect it too.

122
00:07:37,980 --> 00:07:39,980
Do you know what it was that eventually stopped me?

123
00:07:40,980 --> 00:07:41,980
It was fear.

124
00:07:42,980 --> 00:07:44,980
Yes, I was terrified.

125
00:07:45,980 --> 00:07:46,980
Terrified of the person I might become.

126
00:07:47,980 --> 00:07:51,980
Even though all that mattered to me in the end was that I had fun and could do whatever I wanted.

127
00:07:51,980 --> 00:07:55,980
That's when I learned that I needed someone in control.

128
00:07:56,980 --> 00:08:00,980
Not a greedy despot who would rule with tyrannical disregard for the wants and needs of others.

129
00:08:01,980 --> 00:08:04,980
But the rule of a god. One who reigned without ego.

130
00:08:05,980 --> 00:08:09,980
If you hate this world so much, why not join me? We can change the world together.

131
00:08:10,980 --> 00:08:12,980
That's your ego talking now, isn't it?

132
00:08:12,980 --> 00:08:17,980
No. But following one's own ego will become the standard before long.

133
00:08:17,980 --> 00:08:19,980
A standard you too will follow.

134
00:08:28,980 --> 00:08:29,980
Stein!

135
00:08:29,980 --> 00:08:39,980
You can't attack without thinking. She'll keep striking you down if you do.

136
00:08:40,980 --> 00:08:46,980
If this new standard you're talking about does come to pass, what will control my dark side then?

137
00:08:47,980 --> 00:08:50,980
I can never join you in this.

138
00:08:51,980 --> 00:08:53,980
I suppose there's no getting through to you.

139
00:08:53,980 --> 00:08:57,980
I want to tear things apart without losing my soul!

140
00:08:58,980 --> 00:09:00,980
So that's how you choose to use your madness, huh?

141
00:09:04,980 --> 00:09:05,980
What?

142
00:09:05,980 --> 00:09:06,980
So far!

143
00:09:15,980 --> 00:09:16,980
Got her.

144
00:09:17,980 --> 00:09:21,980
But still, he took on way too much damage for just a single hit.

145
00:09:21,980 --> 00:09:25,980
I think I've been overestimating you, Stein.

146
00:09:28,980 --> 00:09:32,980
That flimsy attack is all you could manage after turning down such a gracious invitation.

147
00:09:35,980 --> 00:09:36,980
It's all over.

148
00:09:37,980 --> 00:09:38,980
I think I'll remove your head now.

149
00:09:39,980 --> 00:09:40,980
Spirit, listen. Not a single move.

150
00:09:43,980 --> 00:09:45,980
What the? My tail snake stopped.

151
00:09:46,980 --> 00:09:48,980
I can't move anything.

152
00:09:48,980 --> 00:09:52,980
Soul thread. Diffusion sutures.

153
00:09:53,980 --> 00:09:54,980
What are you talking about?

154
00:09:55,980 --> 00:09:57,980
You haven't even sewn my body to anything yet.

155
00:09:58,980 --> 00:09:59,980
Take a closer look.

156
00:10:00,980 --> 00:10:03,980
The threads are sewn throughout the inside of your body as well.

157
00:10:04,980 --> 00:10:08,980
I'm using them to block every nerve ending you have so you're completely paralyzed.

158
00:10:08,980 --> 00:10:10,980
What are you waiting for?

159
00:10:11,980 --> 00:10:14,980
Why don't you kill me with a hit from your scythe friend there?

160
00:10:15,980 --> 00:10:16,980
You're running out of time, remember?

161
00:10:17,980 --> 00:10:20,980
Controlling such an enormous wavelength takes total concentration.

162
00:10:20,980 --> 00:10:26,980
Focusing on that requires all my energy. I can't move a single finger.

163
00:10:27,980 --> 00:10:29,980
This is pathetic, even for a last ditch effort.

164
00:10:30,980 --> 00:10:33,980
Are you improvising or is this how you always like to fight?

165
00:10:33,980 --> 00:10:41,980
What's your plan? A Wild West shootout the instant you release these threads?

166
00:10:42,980 --> 00:10:44,980
Don't you see how pointless it is?

167
00:10:45,980 --> 00:10:46,980
My snake is already at your neck.

168
00:10:47,980 --> 00:10:50,980
It'll lop your head off before your scythe even has a chance to touch me.

169
00:10:50,980 --> 00:10:56,980
I somehow doubt that wavelength control of this magnitude can last for very long.

170
00:10:57,980 --> 00:11:01,980
Think about it. As soon as it's released you will die.

171
00:11:02,980 --> 00:11:04,980
And the Kishin will be reborn at last.

172
00:11:07,980 --> 00:11:10,980
You don't stand a chance against me now.

173
00:11:11,980 --> 00:11:12,980
That's it.

174
00:11:13,980 --> 00:11:14,980
That?

175
00:11:14,980 --> 00:11:16,980
Yeah, the bag over there.

176
00:11:16,980 --> 00:11:23,980
I wouldn't be surprised if it was an object of worship or something before it sucked up the Kishin's madness.

177
00:11:24,980 --> 00:11:25,980
Now it looks like this.

178
00:11:43,980 --> 00:11:44,980
All set.

179
00:11:46,980 --> 00:11:47,980
This is it.

180
00:11:53,980 --> 00:11:55,980
The black blood is in that syringe!

181
00:11:58,980 --> 00:11:59,980
Take this!

182
00:11:59,980 --> 00:12:00,980
There we go!

183
00:12:05,980 --> 00:12:06,980
What?

184
00:12:09,980 --> 00:12:10,980
Damn!

185
00:12:10,980 --> 00:12:19,980
Who's this mummy guy?

186
00:12:19,980 --> 00:12:20,980
He's been caught in the madness like we were.

187
00:12:20,980 --> 00:12:21,980
Now's our chance.

188
00:12:21,980 --> 00:12:22,980
Right!

189
00:12:25,980 --> 00:12:27,980
Damn it! Not this again.

190
00:12:27,980 --> 00:12:29,980
I'm really getting sick of this guy.

191
00:12:29,980 --> 00:12:31,980
I feel like I'm starting to lose it!

192
00:12:32,980 --> 00:12:33,980
Calm down. Just breathe.

193
00:12:37,980 --> 00:12:41,980
What you're seeing is brought on by the wavelength of the Kishin's madness.

194
00:12:42,980 --> 00:12:44,980
You've felt it plenty of times on the way down here.

195
00:12:44,980 --> 00:12:45,980
It's only a hallucination!

196
00:12:45,980 --> 00:12:49,980
She's got the blood!

197
00:12:50,980 --> 00:12:53,980
This sure hurts more than it did earlier!

198
00:12:53,980 --> 00:12:56,980
As long as I'm aiming for the black blood, the werewolf won't be able to move!

199
00:12:56,980 --> 00:12:58,980
I'll cover you, Blackstar! Go now!

200
00:12:58,980 --> 00:12:59,980
I'm going!

201
00:12:59,980 --> 00:13:00,980
I'm going!

202
00:13:00,980 --> 00:13:03,980
Be careful. The Kishin's madness can make you hallucinate!

203
00:13:03,980 --> 00:13:05,980
No worries on that one. My six sense really sucks!

204
00:13:06,980 --> 00:13:07,980
I can barely feel the madness at all!

205
00:13:08,980 --> 00:13:09,980
Excellent!

206
00:13:10,980 --> 00:13:11,980
It's coming, Erika!

207
00:13:11,980 --> 00:13:12,980
And Janet!

208
00:13:12,980 --> 00:13:14,980
And Janet, the future hurts more than it did earlier!

209
00:13:15,980 --> 00:13:16,980
The future hurts more than it did earlier!

210
00:13:17,980 --> 00:13:19,980
As long as I'm aiming for the black blood, the werewolf won't be able to move!

211
00:13:19,980 --> 00:13:20,980
I'll cover you, Blackstar! Go now!

212
00:13:21,980 --> 00:13:22,980
I'm going!

213
00:13:23,980 --> 00:13:25,980
Be careful. The Kishin's madness can make you hallucinate!

214
00:13:25,980 --> 00:13:28,980
No worries on that one. My six sense really sucks!

215
00:13:28,980 --> 00:13:29,980
I can barely feel the madness at all!

216
00:13:30,980 --> 00:13:31,980
Excellent.

217
00:13:31,980 --> 00:13:32,980
It's coming, Erika!

218
00:13:32,980 --> 00:13:34,980
Enchanted sword mode!

219
00:13:35,980 --> 00:13:38,980
Krivet bomb, krivet crop. Pro krivet, croak, croak!

220
00:13:39,980 --> 00:13:41,980
Try one of my tadpole bombs!

221
00:13:48,980 --> 00:13:50,980
Alright! Don't even try!

222
00:13:53,980 --> 00:13:56,980
It's just a hallucination! Just a hallucination!

223
00:13:59,980 --> 00:14:00,980
Here goes!

224
00:14:00,980 --> 00:14:02,980
Hey! Don't do it! No!

225
00:14:02,980 --> 00:14:04,980
Take this!

226
00:14:05,980 --> 00:14:06,980
What?

227
00:14:08,980 --> 00:14:09,980
Good job, boy!

228
00:14:09,980 --> 00:14:12,980
You didn't find the amphibian getting in my way!

229
00:14:13,980 --> 00:14:14,980
Temple Jackson!

230
00:14:15,980 --> 00:14:17,980
You were a good pet! I won't forget you!

231
00:14:21,980 --> 00:14:25,980
Damn! Don't even think about it! Get the hell away from there, frog girl!

232
00:14:25,980 --> 00:14:26,980
No!

233
00:14:28,980 --> 00:14:29,980
Hurry up, Erika!

234
00:14:30,980 --> 00:14:31,980
You've gotta stop it now, Blackstar!

235
00:14:32,980 --> 00:14:34,980
The enchanted sword mode is at its limit!

236
00:14:35,980 --> 00:14:37,980
But I have to do this, even if it tears me apart!

237
00:14:37,980 --> 00:14:38,980
Even if it tears me apart!

238
00:14:42,980 --> 00:14:43,980
Come on! Hurry!

239
00:14:43,980 --> 00:14:44,980
Please, just go in!

240
00:14:45,980 --> 00:14:47,980
Looks like your time is up, froggy!

241
00:14:47,980 --> 00:14:48,980
Take this!

242
00:14:48,980 --> 00:14:49,980
Take this!

243
00:14:49,980 --> 00:14:50,980
冷!

244
00:14:50,980 --> 00:14:54,980
Eh!

245
00:14:54,980 --> 00:15:17,500
I did it!

246
00:15:17,500 --> 00:15:19,000
We won!

247
00:15:24,980 --> 00:15:36,900
There's no Kishin reviving today.

248
00:15:36,900 --> 00:15:42,080
This is a gamble, and the odds are stacked against us.

249
00:15:42,080 --> 00:15:43,760
We can't hold this forever.

250
00:15:43,760 --> 00:15:48,780
The only way to beat Medusa is to take the offensive somehow and strike at her.

251
00:15:48,780 --> 00:15:52,440
We've come this far, we're just a step away.

252
00:15:52,440 --> 00:16:00,100
The moment those sutures come undone, the fight will start all over again.

253
00:16:00,100 --> 00:16:02,880
And as Medusa said, I'm likely to be the loser.

254
00:16:02,880 --> 00:16:07,380
Her tail is pointed at my throat just a hair's breath away from beheading me.

255
00:16:07,380 --> 00:16:10,400
But right now I can't seem to picture myself being defeated.

256
00:16:10,400 --> 00:16:12,760
All I can imagine is dismembering that witch.

257
00:16:12,760 --> 00:16:18,860
Dissection is what I do best.

258
00:16:18,860 --> 00:16:29,520
My only chance is to roll the dice and hope I win.

259
00:16:29,520 --> 00:16:34,520
What's happening?

260
00:16:34,520 --> 00:16:38,520
What is that?

261
00:16:38,520 --> 00:16:52,020
The Kishin's madness is overflowing.

262
00:16:52,020 --> 00:16:58,520
That means kids' group couldn't stop them.

263
00:16:58,520 --> 00:17:08,520
